    "lawCode": "Amd §627, Cor L (as proposed in S.204 & A.4957)",
    "lawSection": "Correction Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S768\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the correction law, in relation to breast cancer screen-\ning and diagnostic testing for incarcerated individuals\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2024,\nc.570.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by defining \"nationally\nrecognized clinical practice guidelines\" and incorporating these guide-\nlines into breast cancer screenings and diagnostic testing offerings at\nno-cost to incarcerated individuals, unless otherwise recommended by a\nphysician.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nClick here\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 35 of 2024, the Executive stated that changes\nwere necessary to ensure that breast cancer screening and diagnostic\ntesting offerings were responsive to physician recommendations and in\naccordance with national recognized clinical practice guidelines. This\nlegislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter that\naddresses those concerns.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 570 of the Laws of 2024. S.204 passed the\nSenate in February 2024 and A.4957 passed the Assembly in April 2024.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nClick here\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nClick here\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as in\nChapter 570 of the Laws of 2024, which take effect 180 days after signed\ninto law.\n",
